Looking at the code structure and the requirements, I need to implement a FULL JOIN between the Supplier and Product tables using the `sqlgen` library. Since SQLite doesn't natively support FULL JOIN, I'll need to simulate it using a combination of LEFT JOIN and UNION.

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#pragma once

#include <sqlgen.hpp>
#include <sqlgen/sqlite.hpp>
#include <vector>
#include <optional>

namespace full_join_suppliers_products {

struct Supplier {
  sqlgen::PrimaryKey<int> supplier_id;
  std::string name;
};

struct Product {
  sqlgen::PrimaryKey<int> product_id;
  int supplier_id;
  std::string name;
};

struct SupProd {
  std::string supplier_name;
  std::optional<std::string> product_name;
};

/**
 * Returns a vector of SupProd structs, where each struct contains the name of a supplier and the name of a product, if any.
 */
std::vector<SupProd> full_join_suppliers_products() {
  // Connect to the SQLite database
  const auto conn = sqlgen::sqlite::connect("test_db.sqlite");

  // Since SQLite doesn't support FULL JOIN directly, we simulate it using LEFT JOIN and UNION
  // First part: Suppliers with their products (LEFT JOIN)
  auto left_join_query = sqlgen::select(
    sqlgen::column<&Supplier::name>("supplier_name"),
    sqlgen::column<&Product::name>("product_name")
  ).from<Supplier>().left_join<Product>().on(
    sqlgen::column<&Supplier::supplier_id>() == sqlgen::column<&Product::supplier_id>()
  );

  // Second part: Products without suppliers (RIGHT JOIN simulated with reversed LEFT JOIN)
  auto right_join_query = sqlgen::select(
    sqlgen::literal(""),  // Empty supplier name for products without suppliers
    sqlgen::column<&Product::name>("product_name")
  ).from<Product>().left_join<Supplier>().on(
    sqlgen::column<&Product::supplier_id>() == sqlgen::column<&Supplier::supplier_id>()
  ).where(sqlgen::column<&Supplier::supplier_id>().is_null());

  // Combine both parts using UNION to simulate FULL JOIN
  auto full_join_query = left_join_query.union_(right_join_query);

  // Execute the query and return the results
  auto result = sqlgen::read<std::vector<SupProd>>(conn, full_join_query);

  if (result) {
    return result.value();
  } else {
    // Return empty vector if there's an error
    return std::vector<SupProd>{};
  }
}

}  // namespace full_join_suppliers_products
```

This implementation:

1. Connects to the SQLite database "test_db.sqlite"
2. Creates a FULL JOIN simulation using a combination of LEFT JOIN and UNION
3. The first part gets all suppliers with their products (including suppliers without products)
4. The second part gets all products without suppliers
5. Combines both results using UNION to achieve the FULL JOIN effect
6. Returns the results as a vector of SupProd structs

The query ensures that all suppliers and all products are included in the result set, with the product name being optional (std::optional<std::string>) to handle cases where a supplier has no products or a product has no supplier.

